{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790912415,"nonce":"epl/M0mlz7Wnnm9L5er3pCFM+ys=","message":"**Owner's ruling (2026-10-02): the incident provider is generic. No vendor-specific provider ships — not incident.io, not PagerDuty. This comment supersedes the body.**\n\n**What is wrong, restated.** The body's premise — \"without the mapping every later fact becomes a new external incident\" — holds only for a receiver that ignores the key. The generic webhook already carries `incident.id` on every Incident fact (`internal/channels/render/webhookjson/envelope.go:193`, since `d0577ba`), stable for the Incident's life. **That key is the mapping.** A receiver that de-duplicates on it gets one external incident whose later facts are updates; the PagerDuty severity and update-in-place questions are the receiver's field mapping, not oto's code.\n\n**What is left to build.**\n1. **An optional echo.** If an incident-tool receiver's 2xx response body is JSON carrying `external_url` and/or `external_id`, oto records them once per (Incident, channel) as the outbound mapping and shows the link on the Incident's Slack card and page (the card currently has none, per `b963c07`). A response without them is not an error. Nothing else in the response is read — outbound-only (ADR 0052 §5) still holds; this is the receipt of a delivery, like a Slack `ts`, not the incident's state.\n2. **The contract, written down.** Provider docs state: `incident.id` is the de-duplication key; the facts and their meanings (`drawn`, `case_added`, `case_removed`, `quiet`, `active_again`); that `quiet` is a fact, never a resolve, and auto-resolve is the receiver's own rule; that severity, if a tool needs one, comes from the member alerts' own labels in the envelope.\n3. **Recipes** for two tools' generic alert sources, each verified against that tool's current docs at the time of writing — never asserted from memory.\n\n**Done when.** A receiver echoing `external_url` gets it shown on the card and page, idempotently across retries; a receiver echoing nothing behaves exactly as today; a test asserts no request body ever carries a resolve, close or status command; the contract doc and two recipes exist.\n\n**Blocked by.** None — `aa6d18b` is implemented (`d0577ba`).\n\n**Mode.** AFK.","files":null}]}